From 9f4f4b88801f18e0871100c2d86adcaa645b72df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core-loop): stop the release campaign after repeated
 identical failures

The 50-run release gate had no circuit breaker: one systemic defect burned
every remaining attempt (and its credits) before anyone saw the report.

Campaign changes:

- After CORE_LOOP_STOP_AFTER_IDENTICAL_FAILURES consecutive identical
  failures (default 3, floor 2) the campaign exits non-zero and writes
  `earlyStop` plus the offending signature into the report and latest.json
  immediately, so the run that stopped is visible without waiting.
- Every failed attempt now carries a normalized `failureSignature`;
  passes carry null. A pass resets the streak.
- The campaign pins its own AI model tier and honours a request-model
  override on the server, so a stray OPENROUTER_CODING_MODEL in a
  Codespace cannot stall the gate. Generation aborts at 300s.

Failure signatures are `<stage>:<message>` with the stage prefix stripped
from the message, and are aggressively normalized -- a signature that stays
unique per attempt makes the early stop fail OPEN, which defeats the whole
feature. Collapsed: UUIDs, 5+ digit runs, mixed hex ids of 7+ chars
(docker/sandbox container ids are not UUID-shaped), and URL hosts down to
`<sub>.provider.tld` with the path kept. Preview and deployment errors carry
a fresh random sandbox host on every single attempt, so without the host and
hex rules three identical root causes produced three different signatures
and the breaker never tripped.

The stage-prefix strip also matches spaced spellings, so stage `public-url`
against "public URL check failed" no longer yields
`public-url:public URL check failed`.

type-check 0 errors, 629/629 tests pass, lint 0 errors.

